               <img src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="MPPSC Exam Calendar 2026" class="blog-hero-image">
               <div class="blog-body">
                 <h1 class="blog-title">MPPSC Exam Calendar 2026: Your Essential Guide to Upcoming Examinations</h1>
                 <p class="mb-4">
                   The Madhya Pradesh Public Service Commission (MPPSC) has officially released its much-anticipated examination calendar for 2026, bringing clarity and a clear roadmap for thousands of aspirants. Released on December 15, 2025, this calendar outlines the tentative schedule for major competitive and recruitment examinations, including the prestigious State Service Examination, State Forest Service Examination, Assistant Professor posts, and various other departmental recruitments. This is a critical announcement, allowing candidates to meticulously plan their preparation strategies for the upcoming year.
                 </p>

                 <div class="highlight-text">
                   The MPPSC Exam Calendar 2026 is now available on the official website, mppsc.mp.gov.in. Aspirants are strongly advised to download the PDF and align their study plans accordingly.
                 </div>

                 <h2 class="section-title">Key Examinations Covered in the 2026 Calendar</h2>
                 <p>
                   The newly released calendar provides proposed dates for a wide array of examinations. While the schedule is tentative and subject to change based on administrative decisions or court orders, it offers a solid framework for candidates.
                 </p>
                 <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                   <p>✅ State Service Examination (Prelims &amp; Mains)</p>
                   <p>✅ State Forest Service Examination (Prelims &amp; Mains)</p>
                   <p>✅ State Engineering Services Examination</p>
                   <p>✅ Assistant Professor Examinations (various phases)</p>
                   <p>✅ Mining Officer &amp; Assistant Director</p>
                   <p>✅ Deputy Director &amp; Principal Grade-2</p>
                 </div>

                 <h2 class="section-title">Detailed MPPSC Exam Schedule 2026</h2>
                 <p>
                   Here's a comprehensive overview of the key examination dates as per the official MPPSC Exam Calendar 2026:
                 </p>
                 <table>
                   <thead>
                     <tr>
                       <th>Sr. No.</th>
                       <th>Examination Name</th>
                       <th>Proposed Exam Date</th>
                     </tr>
                   </thead>
                   <tbody>
                     <tr>
                       <td>1</td>
                       <td>Assistant Professor (Computer Science) Exam 2025</td>
                       <td>04 January 2026</td>
                     </tr>
                     <tr>
                       <td>2</td>
                       <td>Deputy Director / Assistant Director (Technical) Exam 2025</td>
                       <td>22 February 2026</td>
                     </tr>
                     <tr>
                       <td>3</td>
                       <td>State Engineering Service Exam 2025</td>
                       <td>22 March 2026</td>
                     </tr>
                     <tr>
                       <td>4</td>
                       <td>State Service &amp; State Forest Service Preliminary Exam 2026</td>
                       <td>26 April 2026</td>
                     </tr>
                     <tr>
                       <td>5</td>
                       <td>Assistant Professor Exam 2026 (Phase-1)</td>
                       <td>12 July 2026</td>
                     </tr>
                     <tr>
                       <td>6</td>
                       <td>Assistant Professor Exam 2026 (Phase-2)</td>
                       <td>02 August 2026</td>
                     </tr>
                     <tr>
                       <td>7</td>
                       <td>Assistant Professor Exam 2026 (Phase-3)</td>
                       <td>30 August 2026</td>
                     </tr>
                     <tr>
                       <td>8</td>
                       <td>State Service Main Exam 2026</td>
                       <td>07 – 12 September 2026</td>
                     </tr>
                     <tr>
                       <td>9</td>
                       <td>State Forest Service Main Exam 2026</td>
                       <td>27 September 2026</td>
                     </tr>
                     <tr>
                       <td>10</td>
                       <td>State Service Main Examination 2025</td>
                       <td>To be conducted after the order of Hon'ble High Court (Notify Later)</td>
                     </tr>
                   </tbody>
                 </table>

                 <h2 class="section-title">Important Instructions and Preparation Tips</h2>
                 <p>
                   The MPPSC has also issued crucial guidelines for all candidates. Paying attention to these details can significantly impact your preparation journey.
                 </p>

                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">1. Tentative Nature of the Calendar</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">
                     It's vital to remember that all dates mentioned in the calendar are provisional. The commission reserves the right to make changes due to administrative reasons or judicial directives. Always refer to the official MPPSC website for the latest updates.
                   </div>
                 </div>

                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">2. Separate Notifications for Syllabus and Scheme</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">
                     Detailed examination schemes and syllabi for each specific examination will be released separately. Candidates should not rely solely on the calendar for this information but keep an eye out for individual recruitment advertisements.
                   </div>
                 </div>

                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">3. New Advertisements and Interview Schedules</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">
                     The commission may also issue new advertisements based on requisitions received from various departments. Furthermore, interview schedules for exams where written tests have been completed will be announced independently at a later stage.
                   </div>
                 </div>

                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">4. Strategic Preparation Approach</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">
                     With the calendar now public, aspirants can adopt a focused preparation strategy. For instance, the period from December 2025 to April 2026 can be dedicated primarily to Prelims preparation, followed by an intensive Mains-focused approach from May to September 2026. Integrating optional subjects and essay writing from the outset is also highly recommended.
                   </div>
                 </div>

                 <p>
                   The release of the MPPSC Exam Calendar 2026 is a significant step, providing much-needed clarity for job seekers in Madhya Pradesh. By staying informed, adhering to official announcements, and implementing a well-structured preparation plan, candidates can significantly enhance their chances of success.
                 </p>
                 <p>
                   For the most accurate and up-to-date information, regularly visit the official Madhya Pradesh Public Service Commission website: <a href="https://mppsc.mp.gov.in" target="_blank">mppsc.mp.gov.in</a>.
                 </p>
               </div>
